"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[7668],{18816:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"getCar","desc":"Recovers the Vehicle wrapper for a car model from the module cache, or `nil`\\nif the model is not a live vehicle. The bridge every caller holding only a\\nmodel uses to reach this class\'s methods.","params":[{"name":"model","desc":"","lua_type":"Model"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Vehicle?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":402,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"getCarModel","desc":"Returns the shared car template from `Assets.Vehicles.Car`. This is the\\noriginal, not a clone \u2014 read it for bounding-box measurements, do not modify\\nit.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Model"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":416,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"getRaycastParams","desc":"Returns the shared raycast params used for spawn ground-finding, filtered\\nagainst `Spawner`- and `Water`-tagged instances so neither counts as ground.\\nKept in sync as those tags come and go.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"RaycastParams"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":430,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"getOverlapParams","desc":"Returns the shared overlap params used for the spawn clearance check, filtered\\nthe same way as [Vehicle.getRaycastParams] and capped at one result since any\\nsingle hit is enough to reject a spot.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"OverlapParams"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":444,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"new","desc":"Spawns a vehicle, or returns `nil` if it cannot be placed.\\n\\nPlacement is either the supplied `spawnCFrame` or, for an owned vehicle,\\nresolved from the owner\'s character: a point `SPAWN_DISTANCE` studs ahead is\\nraycast down for ground, and a temporary box the size of the car\'s bounding\\nbox is overlap-tested for clearance. Either failing returns `nil`. This\\nrepeats the check [VehicleController.spawn] already ran on the client, because\\nthe client\'s answer is advisory.\\n\\nSetup, in order:\\n\\n- Clone and tag the model, stamp `OwnerId` and a `SpeedMultiplier` of 1.\\n- Nudge the driver\'s `SeatWeld` via the seat attachment so the character sits\\n  at the wheel rather than at the seat part\'s raw origin.\\n- Wire seat `Occupant` listeners and the enter prompt (itself debounced to one\\n  entry per second).\\n- Assign collision groups: `Details` \u2192 `CarDetail`, `DBO` parts \u2192 `CarBody`,\\n  and every part carrying a `CylindricalConstraint` attachment \u2192 `CarWheel`\\n  with high-friction physical properties so the wheels actually grip.\\n- Parent to the Workspace, then `task.defer` the mass-derived suspension\\n  tuning described on [Vehicle].\\n\\nReturns `nil` without side effects if the model has no `DriverSeat`.","params":[{"name":"config","desc":"Defaults to an unowned vehicle with no placement","lua_type":"VehicleConfig?"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Vehicle?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":493,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"StartTimer","desc":"Arms the idle-despawn timer, which runs `DESPAWN_TIME` after the vehicle is\\nspawned or vacated. [Vehicle:StopTimer] cancels it when someone gets in.\\n\\n:::note\\nThe timer body is commented out, so the vehicle is never actually despawned \u2014\\nthe scheduling is live but the effect is disabled. Re-enabling it requires\\ncalling back into [VehicleService], which is why it was stubbed: this class\\ndoes not import that service.\\n:::","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":791,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"StopTimer","desc":"Cancels a pending idle-despawn timer, if any.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":803,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"OnOccupantChanged","desc":"Handles a seat\'s `Occupant` changing \u2014 the voluntary-exit path, as opposed to\\nthe forced `Eject*` methods.\\n\\nThe enter prompt is toggled to match occupancy, and the idle-despawn timer is\\nstopped while someone is driving and restarted once the vehicle empties.\\n\\nA departing **driver** triggers the full handover described on [Vehicle]: fire\\n`StopControl`, brake, sever the character\'s weld, zero the wheel velocities the\\nclient was commanding, reclaim network ownership through the\\nun-anchor/set/re-anchor dance, place the character on the ground to the car\'s\\nleft, zero their velocity so they do not inherit the car\'s momentum, and stop\\nthe idle engine sound.\\n\\nA departing **passenger** is simply placed on the right-hand side.\\n\\nEither way the character\'s collision is restored on the way out.","params":[{"name":"seat","desc":"The seat whose occupancy changed","lua_type":"VehicleSeat"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":833,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EnterDriverSeat","desc":"Seats a player as the driver. Refuses if the seat is taken, or if `ownerOnly`\\nis set and they are not the owner.\\n\\nGrants the player network ownership of the assembly before seating them \u2014\\nthis is what makes their client the physics authority, and the vehicle must be\\nun-anchored first for the grant to take.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":945,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EnterPassengerSeat","desc":"Seats a player as the passenger. Refuses if there is no passenger seat or it\\nis occupied. Passengers get no network ownership and no control.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":971,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"getSeatedPlayers","desc":"Every player currently seated in this vehicle: the driver (if any)\\nfollowed by the passenger. Only players who boarded through the enter\\nhandlers are known \u2014 engine touch-seated characters are untracked.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ Player }"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":989,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"AttachAttachment","desc":"Clones `attachmentModel` onto the vehicle at the platform attachment named\\n`<attachmentType>Attachment`, welds it to the platform and records it in the\\nslot.\\n\\nRefuses if the slot is already filled \u2014 [VehicleService:equipAttachment]\\nremoves the incumbent first \u2014 and warns and refuses if the model has no\\nPrimaryPart or the named attachment point does not exist.\\n\\nEvery part of the clone is put on the `CarBody` collision group so an\\nattachment cannot collide with the car it is bolted to.","params":[{"name":"attachmentType","desc":"Slot name; also the attachment point prefix","lua_type":"string"},{"name":"attachmentModel","desc":"Template to clone; needs a PrimaryPart","lua_type":"Model"}],"returns":[{"desc":"Whether it was attached","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1022,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"RemoveAttachment","desc":"Destroys the attachment in a slot and clears it.","params":[{"name":"attachmentType","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"`false` if the slot was already empty","lua_type":"boolean"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1086,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"GetAttachment","desc":"Returns the model in a slot, or `nil`.","params":[{"name":"attachmentType","desc":"","lua_type":"string"}],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"Model?"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1108,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"GetAllAttachments","desc":"Returns the live slot-to-model map. Not a copy \u2014 do not mutate it.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"","lua_type":"{ [string]: Model }"}],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1120,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"SetSpeedMultiplier","desc":"Sets the vehicle\'s `SpeedMultiplier` attribute, which the driving client reads\\nevery frame to scale its top speed. Using an attribute rather than a remote\\nmeans the change replicates on its own and applies immediately.\\n\\nClamped to 0..1, so this can only slow a vehicle down; 0 is a full stop.\\nNo-ops if the vehicle has been unparented.","params":[{"name":"multiplier","desc":"0..1","lua_type":"number"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1137,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"Brake","desc":"Stops the vehicle by setting its speed multiplier to 0. The vehicle stays\\nbraked until something restores the multiplier \u2014 entering the driver\'s seat\\nresets it to 1.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1153,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EjectDriver","desc":"Forcibly removes the driver, placing them off the car\'s left side. No-ops if\\nthere is no driver.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1164,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EjectPassenger","desc":"Forcibly removes the passenger, placing them off the car\'s right side. No-ops\\nif there is no passenger.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1181,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EjectAll","desc":"Empties the vehicle \u2014 driver and passenger both.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1197,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"EjectPlayer","desc":"Ejects one specific occupant, whichever seat they are in. No-ops if they are\\nnot aboard.","params":[{"name":"player","desc":"","lua_type":"Player"}],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1211,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"Destroy","desc":"Tears the vehicle down: cancels the despawn timer, destroys the model, and\\ndestroys the Maid \u2014 which also restores collision on any seated characters,\\ndrops the entry from the module cache and destroys `occupiedSignal`.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"method","source":{"line":1227,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[{"name":"Vehicle","desc":"Instance shape of a server-side vehicle.","fields":[{"name":"car","lua_type":"Model","desc":"The spawned car model"},{"name":"driverSeat","lua_type":"VehicleSeat","desc":"Required; construction fails without it"},{"name":"passengerSeat","lua_type":"VehicleSeat","desc":"Optional in practice; may be nil on a one-seat model"},{"name":"body","lua_type":"BasePart","desc":"The car\'s `Body` part"},{"name":"locked","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"While true, nobody may sit down"},{"name":"maid","lua_type":"Maid","desc":"Owns the model and every connection"},{"name":"owner","lua_type":"Player?","desc":"Whose vehicle this is; nil for a public vehicle"},{"name":"occupiedDriver","lua_type":"Player?","desc":"Current driver"},{"name":"occupiedPassenger","lua_type":"Player?","desc":"Current passenger"},{"name":"occupiedSignal","lua_type":"Signal","desc":"(player, \\"StartControl\\" | \\"StopControl\\")"},{"name":"attachments","lua_type":"{ [string]: Model }","desc":"Slot type to attached model"},{"name":"ownerOnly","lua_type":"boolean","desc":"Restrict the driver\'s seat to `owner`"},{"name":"lastSatInCar","lua_type":"number","desc":"Server time of the last seat entry; debounces the prompt"},{"name":"timerThread","lua_type":"thread?","desc":"Pending idle-despawn timer"}],"source":{"line":147,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}},{"name":"VehicleConfig","desc":"Construction options for [Vehicle.new]. Supplying `spawnCFrame` bypasses\\nplacement resolution entirely, which is how a vehicle can be spawned somewhere\\nno player is standing.","fields":[{"name":"owner","lua_type":"Player?","desc":"Whose vehicle this is; also the reference point for auto-placement"},{"name":"ownerOnly","lua_type":"boolean?","desc":"Restrict the driver\'s seat to the owner (default false)"},{"name":"spawnCFrame","lua_type":"CFrame?","desc":"Explicit placement, skipping the ground/clearance search"}],"source":{"line":459,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}}],"name":"Vehicle","desc":"Manages a single vehicle instance: spawning, seat occupancy,\\ncollision setup, despawn timer, and cleanup.\\n\\nOne instance wraps one car model. Instances are registered in a module-level\\n`Model \u2192 Vehicle` cache so any code holding just the model can recover the\\nwrapper with [Vehicle.getCar] \u2014 that is how [VehicleService] gets from its\\n`player \u2192 Model` map to the behaviour on this class.\\n\\n### Network ownership is the whole design\\n\\nPhysics is simulated by the driver\'s client. Taking the driver\'s seat hands\\nthat client network ownership of the assembly; leaving it reclaims ownership\\nfor the server. The reclaim sequence in [Vehicle:OnOccupantChanged] is\\ndeliberately fussy \u2014 sever the character\'s weld first, zero the wheel\\nvelocities the client was driving, then un-anchor \u2192 `SetNetworkOwner(nil)` \u2192\\nre-anchor, and only 0.1s later zero the assembly velocity and release. Each\\nstep exists to stop a specific artefact: dragging the character with the car,\\nwheels spinning forever at their last commanded velocity, and the vehicle\\nclipping through the floor as the server resolves a position it did not\\nsimulate.\\n\\n### Collision groups\\n\\nSet up once at require time: `CarDetail` ignores both the body and the wheels,\\nand `CarWheel` ignores `CarBody` \u2014 the constraints already position the wheels,\\nso letting them collide with the body only produces jitter.\\n\\n### Suspension\\n\\nSpring stiffness and damping are computed from the assembly\'s real mass, one\\nframe after parenting (`task.defer`, because `AssemblyMass` is not meaningful\\nuntil then). Stiffness is sized so the car sags exactly\\n`SUSPENSION_TARGET_SAG` studs at rest, and damping from the standard\\n`2\u03b6\u221a(km)` relation at `SUSPENSION_DAMPING_RATIO`. Tuning against measured mass\\nrather than fixed numbers means adding attachments or passengers does not\\nbottom the car out.\\n\\n### Ejection\\n\\nEvery exit path routes through the same helper, which projects the exit\\ndirection onto the XZ plane (so a flipped car does not eject downward),\\nraycasts for ground, falls back to the vehicle\'s roof if there is none, and\\nclamps to `MIN_EJECT_Y` as a last resort against dropping players through the\\nworld.\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Vehicle \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks enable\\nit deliberately.\\n\\nCopyright (c) 2026 firebit. All rights reserved.\\nfirebit/murder-escape - proprietary and confidential.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":57,"path":"src/Server/Features/Vehicle/Class/Vehicle.luau"}}')}}]);